 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-027
 **Description:** Running Exp 4015 either writes `blocked_arc_offline_env_unavailable` when the offline Arcade cannot load, or records every attempted remaining non-spatial candidate and its observed dynamics before pruning. A successful L1 solve MUST use `success: fifth_game_solved_<game>_at_action<n>`, set `dynamics_induced=true`, set `exploration_actions_used>0`, compute `actions_vs_baseline` from the selected game's L0 baseline reference, and confirm the solve through `levels_completed`; a no-solve run MUST use `complete: fifth_game_no_solve_<reason>` while preserving the observed transitions, induced mechanic, verifier-pruner decisions, and candidate outcomes for all attempted games.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-028: ARC-AGI-3 ArcMemo Solve Transfer V4
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4016 as an ArcMemo solve-loop transfer check against the current milestone's new content, preferring Exp 4015's fifth-game solve, otherwise Exp 4014's higher-level advance, otherwise a re-held-out solved level. The experiment MUST first confirm the offline Arcade precondition, build concept memory records from banked solved-game mechanics using `{name, when_it_applies, effect}`, require the target to share structure with at least two same-family banked concepts before attempting transfer, compare cold-start solving against concept-memory-seeded solving at equal offline perception, count real `env.step` actions and reset attempts to the first `levels_completed` increment in each arm, record the concrete concept retrieved and reused, and write `results/experiment_4016_arcmemo_solve_transfer_v4.json` with bare fields `solve_transfer_win`, `actions_cold_start`, `actions_with_memory`, `attempts_cold_start`, `attempts_with_memory`, `target_game`, `concept_reused`, `positive_control_shared_structure`, `real_env_confirmed`, `random_seed`, `honest_verdict`, `duration_s`, and `inference_substrate`.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-028
+**Description:** Running Exp 4016 either writes `blocked_arc_offline_env_unavailable` when the offline Arcade cannot load, reports `complete: arcmemo_solve_no_transfer_positive_control_failed` when the selected target does not share structure with at least two banked concepts, stops honestly when no replayable retrieved concept exists for the chosen target, or completes an honest two-arm solve-loop comparison. A transfer win MUST use `success: arcmemo_solve_transfer_v4_<a_cold>to<a_mem>_actions` only when both arms are confirmed by the real offline environment and the memory-seeded arm uses fewer actions or reset attempts than cold start; otherwise it MUST use `complete: arcmemo_solve_no_transfer_to_new_content_<reason>` while preserving measured action and attempt counts.
